{"timestamp": "2026-10-18T11:21:34.048Z", "source_line": 18, "record": {"type": "custom_tool_call_output", "id": "ctco_01a14ebe-de60-7960-9333-b39a39e70748", "call_id": "call_028543a649a0475b88bc5ce22b3375d2", "output": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"}, {"type": "input_text", "text": "[{\"name\": \"mcp__code_review__pull_requests_checks\", \"description\": \"Read CI diagnostics for a pull or merge request through the Codex backend. For discovery, pass pullRequest and the selected account, if provided. Use the returned providerGuidance for further reads. Preserve the selected account a\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__compile_latex_document\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nCompile a saved TeX document or local multifile project with the built-in LaTeX editor and return diagnostics. Local projects compile their remembered main document with supporting sources, styles\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__create_thread\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nCreate a separate task only when the user explicitly asks for a new task. The prompt appears as a user-visible message in the new task. Write clear, cohesive, human-readable prose. Use project for\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__create_worktree\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nCreate and attach a managed Git worktree on this chat's host. Subagent worktrees attach to the top-level parent chat. If registration fails, call attach_worktree with its returned workspace direct\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__handoff_thread\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nMove another Codex thread and its associated git state between its checkout and Codex worktree on its current host. Running threads are interrupted before handoff. Omit destinationHostId for this \"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__list_archived_threads\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nList one page of archived Codex tasks or ChatGPT conversations. Codex is the default source; omit hostId to use the calling task's host. ChatGPT archives require a local desktop caller; use source\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__list_artifacts\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nList this chat's attached pull requests, active worktrees, archived worktrees, and other saved attachments. Returns each supported attachment's type, identity, payload, and creation time; older ho\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__list_projects\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nList local, remote, and ChatGPT projects available for task creation, including whether each project is a Git repository. Use a returned projectId with create_thread. This tool is part of plugin `\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__move_thread_to_project\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nMove a thread into an existing project. Use source chatgpt for ChatGPT conversations, which require a ChatGPT project. Codex threads stay on their execution host; local threads can also join ChatG\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__read_thread\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nRead recent status and turn summaries for one thread or chat without opening it. Use page cursors from earlier responses to read older turns. This tool is part of plugin `codex-app-tools`.\\n\\nexec t\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__send_message_to_thread\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nSend a follow-up prompt to an existing thread or chat only when the user explicitly authorizes messaging that task. Typed or spoken authorization counts. Authorization must come directly from the \"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__set_thread_archived\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nArchive or unarchive a Codex thread or ChatGPT conversation in the background. Specify hostId only for Codex threads. This tool is part of plugin `codex-app-tools`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\nd\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__set_thread_read_state\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nMark an existing Codex thread or ChatGPT conversation read or unread. Specify hostId only for Codex threads. ChatGPT read state is local to the current window and does not persist across app resta\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__update_sidebar_preferences\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nChange the shared sort setting for Recents and project chats, or sort pinned items separately, across Codex and Work. Grouping applies to one surface. Omitted preferences stay unchanged. Returns t\"}, {\"name\": \"mcp__codex_app__wait_threads\", \"description\": \"Tools provided by the Codex app.\\n\\nWait for the first of up to eight Codex threads to complete or need attention. New user input ends the wait early. Use timeoutMs: 0 for an immediate snapshot. Commentary never wakes the wait. An u\"}]"}, {"type": "input_text", "text": "{\"chunk_id\": \"795169\", \"wall_time_seconds\": 0.373925, \"exit_code\": 0, \"original_token_count\": 825, \"output\": \"\\r\\nPath\\r\\n----\\r\\nD:\\\\Project\\\\AgenticCyberDog\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : ssh.exe\\r\\nSource : C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\OpenSSH\\\\ssh.exe\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : ssh-keygen.exe\\r\\nSource : C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\OpenSSH\\\\ssh-keygen.exe\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : config\\r\\nLength : 190\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : id_ed25519\\r\\nLength : 411\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : id_ed25519.pub\\r\\nLength : 100\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : known_hosts\\r\\nLength : 2856\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : known_hosts.old\\r\\nLength : 2675\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : .sandbox\\r\\nLength : \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : .sandbox-bin\\r\\nLength : \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : .sandbox-secrets\\r\\nLength : \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : .tmp\\r\\nLength : \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : ambient-suggestions\\r\\nLength : \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nName   : archived_sessions\\r\\nLe